{"title":"Mexican Mathematics Olympiad","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>The <b>Mexican Mathematics Olympiad</b> (also known as the <b>Olimpiada Mexicana de Matemáticas</b>, or OMM for short), is a series of tests that Mexican students participate.  The contests gradually increase in difficulty and are used as a selection process for Mexico's <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"IMO\">IMO</a> team, much like the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"AMC\">AMC</a> in the United States.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Structure\">Structure</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mexican_Mathematics_Olympiad&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Structure\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In each Mexican state, there are three contests of increasing difficulty.  From these three, six students are selected per state to take the national contest.  Advancing participants are trained until six of them are selected to represent Mexico in the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"IMO\">IMO</a>.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Contests\">Contests</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mexican_Mathematics_Olympiad&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Contests\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li>State Contests\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=OMM_Elimination_Exam\" title=\"OMM Elimination Exam\">OMM Elimination Exam</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=OMM_Semifinal_Exam\" title=\"OMM Semifinal Exam\">OMM Semifinal Exam</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=OMM_Final_Exam\" title=\"OMM Final Exam\">OMM Final Exam</a></li></ul></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mexico_National_Olympiad\" title=\"Mexico National Olympiad\">Mexico National Olympiad</a></li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Website\">Website</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mexican_Mathematics_Olympiad&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Website\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.ommenlinea.org\">Official Website (in Spanish)</a>\n<ul><li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.ommenlinea.org/actividades/concursos/concursos-estatales/\">Past State Contests (in Spanish)</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.ommenlinea.org/actividades/concursos/concurso-nacional/\">Past National Contests (in Spanish)</a></li></ul></li></ul>\n<p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Mexican_Mathematics_Olympiad&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017183524\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.012 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.025 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 22/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 325/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 0/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.859      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    5.859      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:16679:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017183524 and revision id 97396. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n 